Real-NVMe Stability Qualification
================================
	Primary path: API + SPDK. Compatibility path: FUSE + SPDK.
	Validate through NVFUSE, not only raw-device I/O. Keep failed volumes and
	logs; recovery checks must reopen the original volume without formatting.

	[ ] Review the 24-hour soak launched on 2026-11-13 after it finishes.
	    - Sequential API/FUSE ownership, journaling enabled, 95-97% usage.
	    - Record completed fill/verify/delete cycles, peak usage, actual file
	      and directory counts, sizes, bytes written/read, and all errors.
	    - Confirm full API bulk-data verification, full small-file verification
	      across both interfaces, and sampled FUSE bulk-data verification.
	    - Check rename/hardlink/truncate, clean reopen/remount, and space/inode
	      reclamation after deletion, accounting for retained audit roots.
	    - Check memory/resource growth across cycles; add periodic process
	      memory sampling if the existing logs do not establish this.
	    - Confirm final driver/hugepage restoration and NVMe SMART health.
	[ ] Inject process termination at journal commit/checkpoint boundaries;
	    reopen without formatting and verify committed data and namespace.
	[ ] Separately test actual power-loss/reset durability and recovery;
	    clean remounts and process termination do not establish this.
	[ ] Test complete block ENOSPC and inode exhaustion, including concurrent
	    allocation, partial-write/error semantics, deletion, and space reuse.
	    First replace primary-path exhaustion assertions with safe errors;
	    the 95-97% soak reserve intentionally excludes complete exhaustion.
	[ ] Inject I/O errors, completion delays/timeouts, and device loss during
	    filesystem operations; verify error propagation and retained-volume
	    recovery without silently retrying through a new format.
	[ ] Stress concurrent mutation in the same directories, including name
	    collisions, rename/unlink/link races, open-file deletion, and truncate
	    versus I/O, with content, link-count, and exact-namespace checks.
	[ ] Repeat long-duration qualification after fixes; a successful short
	    smoke run or elapsed runtime alone is not a stability pass.

